{
  "name": "I Want a Better Garage Interior, Where Do I Start?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you're ready to give your garage interior a serious upgrade – awesome! It can feel like a big task, but breaking it down makes it much more manageable. Here’s a good path to follow:",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "**Step 1: Declutter and Deep Clean.** Honestly, this is the most crucial first step. Get rid of anything you don’t need or use. Then, give the whole space a thorough cleaning. You’ll be amazed at how much better it looks already!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "**Step 2: Low-Cost Impact Upgrades.** Once it’s clean, think about some easy wins. A fresh coat of paint on the walls can brighten things up significantly. Swapping out old light fixtures for bright LED lighting makes a huge difference. You might also add some freestanding storage units or even repurpose old furniture to get things organized without breaking the bank.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4",
      "text": "**Step 3: Consider More Involved Upgrades.** If you’re ready to go further, this is where things like floor coatings (epoxy, for example) come in. Think about wall organization systems, built-in cabinetry, or even overhead storage racks. The typical sequence is surface prep, then flooring, allowing for curing, and finally installing your chosen storage and accessories. For these bigger steps, especially things like floor coatings or custom systems, you might find that having a professional like HH Remodeling LLC step in can ensure everything is installed perfectly and lasts for years.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
